/** @mainpage

This suite exercises the tsf-* security libraries against the Test Agent
it runs on:

- @ref cybersec-devtool - compilers and make on an agent (tsf-devtool);
- @ref cybersec-kernel - kernel interfaces, modules and hardening
  posture (tsf-kernel);
- @ref cybersec-cybersec - binary hardening, banned calls and network
  exposure (tsf-cybersec);
- @ref cybersec-fuzz - a fuzzing campaign end to end (tsf-fuzz);
- @ref cybersec-tls - what an endpoint agrees to and whether a client
  checks (tsf-tls).

Every test plants what it is about to look for. The assertion is that
the scanner reports the planted defect, so a scanner that reports
nothing is the failure - which is the opposite of how a suite against a
real product reads, and the right way round for a suite whose subject is
the scanners themselves.

*/
